CheckoutStatus.description:
Where a checkout stands: `created` waiting for the customer; `awaiting_payment` paid and being
confirmed, or failed and open to a retry; `completed` paid, its subscription created;
`expired` past its `expires_at` unpaid; `cancelled` cancelled before it was paid.

ExtraKind.description:
What an item of a card prices: `base`, the fixed fees billed on the card's period, summed;
`per_seat`, per seat of a managed quantity; `usage`, metered usage; `one_time`, a fee billed
once; `credit_pack`, a pack of credit; `recurring`, a fixed fee billed on its own period.

PaymentState.description:
Where a payment is: `ready`, to be sent to the provider; `pending`, waiting for the provider;
`settled`; `cancelled`; `failed`; `refunded`, settled then wholly clawed back (a refund, a
chargeback, a lost dispute).

PaymentStatus.description:
What is paid of an invoice: `unpaid`, `partially_paid`, `paid`; `errored`, its last payment
failed; `processing`, a payment is accepted by the provider, not settled yet (direct debit);
`carried`, below the minimum charge, owed on the customer's next invoice and paid with it.

PlanStatus.description:
Where a plan is in its life: `draft`, never published; `active`, published and sold;
`inactive`, published but off pricing pages and checkout links (no v2 write sets it);
`archived`, no longer sold, its subscriptions keeping it.

ReversalKind.description:
Why a payment was clawed back: `refund`, given back; `chargeback`, by the card holder's bank;
`debtor_recall`, a direct debit recalled by the debtor; `insufficient_funds`;
`mandate_invalid`, the direct debit mandate was revoked or invalid; `returned`, the bank
returned it; `dispute`, lost in a dispute; `other`. `chargeback`, `debtor_recall` and
`dispute` leave the invoice paid and mark the payment disputed; any other makes the amount due
again.

warnings.description:
Read whole, what it is sold with as it stands: `plan_sold_for_mismatch` (the plan is sold
for another resource type than the subscription's resource, or for the customer),
`metric_not_attributed` (its resource never bills some metrics it prices).

SubscriptionGrantStatus.description:
Where a subscription's grant stands: `scheduled` its window, or the subscription, has not
started; `active`; `ended` its window is over or it ended with the subscription;
`withdrawn` the subscription never started.

TaxExemption.description:
Why a tax applies at no rate: `reverse_charge`, the tax is due by the customer;
`tax_exempt`, the customer is exempt; `not_registered`, no tax applied and no reason is known
(no country, tax resolved outside Meteroid…); `export`, sold outside the seller's territory;
`no_vat_territory`, taxable where VAT does not apply in the seller's own territory.

TrialStatus.description:
Where a subscription's trial stands: `active` running; `converted` billing started;
`cancelled` the subscription ended with it; `switched` it moved plan; `awaiting_payment`
converted without a payment method, billing waiting for its opening invoice's payment;
`awaiting_decision` ended with a manual end action, nothing billed until it is decided.

UsageAtZero.description:
What a customer's usage does once the credit it can use runs out: what each subscription's
plan says, or always or never stop, for this customer. `follow_plan`: as each plan says;
`always_pause`: usage stops; `never_pause`: usage goes on, billed.
